# What NOT to upload to the EAS build server.
#
# THIS FILE MUST LIVE AT THE GIT ROOT. EAS archives from the repository root,
# not from the Expo project directory, so an .easignore inside apps/mobile/ is
# never read. Mine was there for two builds: the archive stayed 1.1 GB, and the
# 987 MB of source PDFs sitting inside the project root went to the build
# worker for Metro to crawl.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for uploads rather than adding to it, so
# everything that must stay out has to be repeated here.

# ── the corpus: 987 MB of source PDFs, used by no build step ─────────────────
# The app reads exactly one content file — apps/mobile/assets/content/
# studymate.db — which the export produces and which IS uploaded.
content/
dist/
apps/api/
tools/

# ── build output, caches, native projects EAS regenerates ────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/.expo/
.expo/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── local noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
.git/
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.octogent/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── secrets, belt and braces ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env
!.env.example
*.keystore
*.jks
